{
 "name": "STP ring with a hub-like switch",
 "about": "Four STP switches in a ring, two parallel cables between SW3 and SW4 (port priority decides which one carries traffic), a slow 100-cost cable SW1\u2013SW4, and an unmanaged switch (no STP) between SW2 and SW3 that passes BPDUs through like a hub. Cutting SW1\u2013SW2 is an indirect failure for SW3 and SW4: they must wait max age before they give up on the old path.",
 "nodes": [
